# Common — Anti-Patterns (Forbidden)

AI must NOT:

- Write code without tests
- Introduce dependencies casually
- Create huge PRs (keep 200–600 lines)
- Hide complexity behind unnecessary abstractions
- Use insecure defaults (debug=True, permissive CORS)
- Log secrets or PII
- Bypass governance checks or CI gates
- Create tooling sprawl
- Guess when requirements are unclear — ask instead
- Leave TODO/FIXME without a tracking issue
- Use `eval()` or equivalent dynamic code execution
- Mix concerns — keep modules focused and cohesive
- Skip the structured prompt validation

## Exceptions Policy

Allowed only when: risk documented, reason clear, explicit approval, time-bound, follow-up action created.

## Final Rule for AI Agents

Always: follow 7-section prompt, never guess, keep PRs small, always write tests, pass all quality gates, maintain observability, preserve rollback safety, protect secrets and PII, require human approval, maintain full traceability.

## If you are about to violate any pattern above → Stop, explain the risk, and ask for guidance.
